    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0455" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg375"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Swenson to Mr. Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 284.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copies
                    of my notes to the foreign office in the military service case of James Nelson,
                    which has not previously been reported to the Department.</p>
                <p>Under date of March 22, 1902, the minister of foreign affairs advised me that, in
                    accordance with my request, Mr. Nelson’s sentence had been commuted to a
                    fine.</p>
                <p>This was satisfactory to Mr. Nelson, and permitted him to proceed on his homeward
                    journey without further interruption.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S.
                    Swenson.</hi></signed></closer>





